# Known background structural-variant regions of the R64 reference: intervals
# where the R64 assembly does not represent common lab-strain genomes, so
# alignments and junctions here are reference artifacts, not biology.
# A junction overlapping any interval is flagged `background_sv` by Station C
# (pool-gate) and demoted to demote_orthogonal_evidence on BOTH tracks.
#
# chrIII SRD1 flank-A (Kevin Roy, adjudicated 2026-08-20): the segment
# distal to chrIII:148,614 is deleted and replaced by Ty1 in real strain
# genomes (yKR888 T2T assembly; SGTC WGS_lineage_T2T CHRIII_MECHANISM_
# CONSENSUS_20260625 — 17 split-junction ONT reads join donor-end 148,618 to
# flank-B 151,520/151,669; window is 0x in founders DHY214/X303 and yKR888/
# yKR901). Independently reproduced in BY4742 cDNA (Chanfreau planning/730:
# terminal-clip bridging manufactures canonical-looking 1.9-2.9 kb "introns"
# chrIII:148,615-151,517 and 149,817-151,668). Interval covers both observed
# donor ends and both flank-B endpoints with ~100 bp margin.
#
# Columns: chrom  start  end  name   (BED, 0-based half-open)
chrIII	148500	151800	SRD1_flankA_Ty1_background_SV
